 "title": "The logical Cartesian plane is a taxicab plane",
 "subject": "What distance the product of two logical number lines measures",
 "conclusion": "In the product law of two parity laws, a knot of each axis joined at a corner is a knot, so bond distance is at most the sum of the axis distances minus one. The product of two two-way threads has no ends, so its bond distance is within constants of taxicab distance and its bond balls grow quadratically: a plane of dimension two built from two lines.",
